    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Gender-based violence (GBV) or violence against women and girls (VAWG), is a global pandemic that affects 1 in 3 women in their lifetime, according to a 2019 report by the World Bank. In efforts to combat this issue locally, faculty members of the Aga Khan University School of Nursing and Midwifery, AKU-SONAM, recently conducted a Community Mobilizers' Training of Trainers on GBV, in the Chitral region, led by Professor Dr Tazeen Saeed Ali, associate dean of research and innovation, Zohra Jetha, senior instructor, and Ahad Salman, research specialist at the School.",
